content:
{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Tara Singh (E035, Data Analyst, Operations) asks how many bereavement days she is entitled to after her grandfather's death on Saturday 2026-11-14, with the funeral in Dayton next Tuesday (2026-11-24). She also asks whether she must use PTO for it. I checked POL-PTO-01 (PTO, 20 days/yr, booking in HR portal, 2 weeks' notice for 3+ consecutive days) and POL-SICK-01 (10 sick days, doctor's note rules). Neither mentions bereavement leave, so I could not answer from policy. Please advise on bereavement entitlement and whether PTO or other leave applies."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "I'm very sorry for your loss, Tara.\n\nI checked our PTO and sick leave policies, and neither covers bereavement leave, so I can't tell you how many bereavement days you get or whether you must use PTO. I've passed your question to the HR team with the details (your grandfather's passing on Saturday and the funeral in Dayton next Tuesday), and they will come back to you on the entitlement and how to record the time off.\n\nIf you need to book time off before you hear back, the HR portal is where PTO is booked.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-PTO-01",
  "POL-SICK-01"
 ]
}
